Bluetooth (VESC Express)␀␀␀␀Bluetooth needs no CAN wiring: this display connects to a VESC Express the same way VESC Tool does. The CAN settings on the previous screen only apply in CAN mode.␀Bluetooth adapter␀␀␀Round trip␀␀Drops / timeouts / stale␀␀␀␀Packet size (MTU)␀␀␀An adapter that does not advertise its name shows as '?'. Only one device can hold a VESC Express link at a time - disconnect VESC Tool on the phone first.␀Target␀␀Controller is behind the adapter␀␀␀␀On: requests are forwarded across the adapter's CAN bus to Target VESC ID %u, which is how a VESC Express is normally wired. Off: the adapter itself is the target.␀The quick-action drawer and the cruise/profile readout need the LISP script from this firmware's lisp/main.lisp (2026-09 or newer) on the controller - older scripts only answer over CAN.␀␀Supermoto␀␀␀Lamborghini␀Classic_Max␀Classic Max␀vesc_ui␀I (%lu) %s: init: once=%lldms build=%lldms TOTAL=%lldms (theme=%d/%d)
